WEBVTT

00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:03.710
This girl has stood upon the boundary,

00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:07.580
and now she surely has a 
painful life ahead of her.

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:12.520
No matter how warped 
and hardened it might be,

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:16.900
I want her to find human happiness in the end.

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:23.660
You know what you must do 
to ensure that, do you not?

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:32.000
Hello?

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.750
It's me, Zohei.

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:37.770
<i>Sorry for the short notice,</i>

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:41.130
<i>but I need to talk to you about my grandson.</i>

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:41.810
Yes?

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:46.670
<i>I thought it might help him if he 
could stay with you for a while.</i>

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:49.180
<i>Mind having a look at him?</i>

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:50.780
Certainly.

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:56.310
But would you be willing to 
accept a condition in exchange?

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:13.670
<i>Malevolent Spirits</i>

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:32.000
<b>Arrangement</b>

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:35.250
<b>List of Kunato Hyoma Supporters</b>

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:35.250
<b>-san</b>

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:35.250
<b>• Nagi</b>

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:35.250
<b>• Kagami</b>

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:35.250
<b>• Suzuri</b>

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:35.250
<b>• Haori</b>

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:35.250
<b>• Kushige</b>

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:35.250
<b>• Yu</b>

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:37.260
<b>• Yu</b>

00:02:38.230 --> 00:02:41.760
<i>I've managed to return to square one.</i>

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:46.470
<i>No... Things aren't quite 
as they were from the start.</i>

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:48.270
<i>At the very least,</i>

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:51.420
<i>I do feel more of a connection here</i>

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:54.420
<i>in the Nagatsuki household 
than I've ever felt before.</i>

00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:57.560
<i>But my duty now is to ascertain</i>

00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:04.040
<i>whether these are indeed tsukumogami 
in whom I can place my full trust.</i>

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:08.520
Hyoma-san!

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:11.340
Did you really get everyone's signatures?!

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:21.050
Sorry to burst in like that!

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:23.900
I don't mind that at all.

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:30.380
Your information is accurate.

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:32.810
I've caused you a great deal of trouble.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:35.630
Would you accept an apology for my rudeness,

00:03:35.630 --> 00:03:38.200
and allow me to make a new first impression?

00:03:40.630 --> 00:03:44.030
Sorry! You're just always so uptight.

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:47.340
You're going to give yourself 
a heart attack one day!

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:53.200
You shouldn't laugh when you're already 
out of breath from running.

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:54.830
I... I'm okay.

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:55.900
Okay.

00:03:56.510 --> 00:03:59.590
Here's to a full year together, then.

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:03.830
Yes.

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:07.370
I appreciate your hospitality.

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:14.730
<b>Wind
 Forest
 Fire
 Mountain</b>

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:12.270
We're really going to tell him already?

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:14.730
Yeah. I mean, he met the conditions.

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:19.920
Yu-chan only signed because she felt bad 
about the trouble she caused him, right?

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:23.900
And I'm not sure the two of them 
will like having this sprung on them.

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:27.210
We do have a whole year ahead of us.

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:30.370
Why not allow for a longer grace period?

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:37.880
<b>List of Kunato Hyoma Supporters</b>

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:37.880
<b>-san</b>

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:37.880
<b>• Nagi</b>

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:37.880
<b>• Kagami</b>

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:37.880
<b>• Suzuri</b>

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:37.880
<b>• Haori</b>

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:37.880
<b>• Kushige</b>

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:37.880
<b>• Yu</b>

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:34.910
Whatever we do, we're already 
on record as supporting him.

00:04:34.910 --> 00:04:37.880
Over a pretty damned short period, at that.

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:40.660
I'm saying the time's ripe.

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:42.250
Right, Kushige?

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:46.650
Haori's come to the same conclusion.

00:04:49.750 --> 00:04:51.440
Oh, that's right.

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:54.760
We cook dinner in shifts here.

00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:56.650
Can you cook, Hyoma-san?

00:04:57.300 --> 00:04:59.430
I've cooked many times at home.

00:05:01.170 --> 00:05:03.150
Though I can't make anything 
especially complicated.

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:05.030
Hey, that's okay.

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:07.300
Nagi can't make anything but beer snacks...

00:05:15.390 --> 00:05:17.320
Hyoma-san, Botan...

00:05:17.720 --> 00:05:20.960
There's something we must tell you.

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:22.300
Would you join us in the great hall?

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:29.180
It regards an arrangement 
I made with Zohei-san

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:31.680
in exchange for taking Hyoma-san in.

00:05:32.190 --> 00:05:33.100
What?

00:05:33.950 --> 00:05:38.570
We of the Nagatsuki tsukumogami 
share a single purpose.

00:05:38.570 --> 00:05:44.190
The request to have you stay here aligned 
perfectly with our motivations in that regard.

00:05:46.750 --> 00:05:51.200
We agreed to allow you 
to observe us for one year,

00:05:51.560 --> 00:05:55.700
and made a request of Zohei-san in turn.

00:05:56.110 --> 00:06:02.960
That we, too, would be allowed 
to spend the year evaluating you.

00:06:04.600 --> 00:06:06.950
Wait! Not again—

00:06:07.390 --> 00:06:08.880
Quiet now.

00:06:10.940 --> 00:06:12.230
I don't understand.

00:06:12.880 --> 00:06:14.550
Why would you want to do that?

00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:17.180
And why reveal it now?

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:24.570
We intended to spend the year evaluating 
whether or not we find you worthy.

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:29.180
But you've made us do something 
fairly similar in just three days.

00:06:29.570 --> 00:06:33.140
So I thought the time was ripe 
to reveal everything to you.

00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:37.960
This is our purpose...

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:43.340
<b>Celebrate!

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:43.340
<b>Welcome!</b>

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:50.590
<b>Celebrate!

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:50.590
<b>Welcome!</b>

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:50.590
<b>Long Life</b>

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:50.590
The first step to finding a man 
worthy of marriage to our mistress.

00:06:52.280 --> 00:06:53.500
Is this...

00:06:59.230 --> 00:07:00.980
<b>Celebrate!

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:04.000
Don't get the wrong idea!

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:07.850
I-It's a silly prank they play sometimes.

00:07:07.850 --> 00:07:09.530
Please... don't get the wrong idea!

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:11.990
Don't you say another word!

00:07:12.250 --> 00:07:13.860
C'mon, ma'am!

00:07:13.860 --> 00:07:16.330
We're doin' this for real!

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:17.830
Right, Kushige?

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:22.250
H-He's right! We're really trying our best!

00:07:24.250 --> 00:07:26.710
With Suzuki-kun in third grade...

00:07:24.250 --> 00:07:27.250
<b>Suzuki-kun (9)</b>

00:07:27.250 --> 00:07:29.320
With Tanaka-kun in seventh grade...

00:07:27.250 --> 00:07:32.010
<b>Tanaka-kun (13)</b>

00:07:29.320 --> 00:07:31.190
We evaluated both of them very earnestly!

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:35.640
But, but, but... I told you 
to stop all that, didn't I?!

00:07:36.920 --> 00:07:39.830
<i>I</i> rejected them both, of course.

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:46.020
I'm afraid it's unavoidable, Botan.

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:54.910
We manifested in objects tasked with 
seeking a happy match for their owner.

00:07:55.260 --> 00:07:57.080
Tasked with...

00:07:57.080 --> 00:07:57.910
Yes.

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:01.160
We don't originate from individual objects.

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:07.670
We are from a single trousseau—
objects offered by the bride upon marriage.

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:13.340
And so we have a purpose 
we are driven to fulfill.

00:08:13.980 --> 00:08:15.080
Hyoma-san...

00:08:15.080 --> 00:08:17.070
In addition to the purpose you assigned them,

00:08:17.070 --> 00:08:20.970
our signatures signify that you 
passed our evaluation.

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:25.660
In a <i>purely</i> provisional fashion.

00:08:25.660 --> 00:08:27.440
You shut up, Yu!

00:08:27.880 --> 00:08:31.160
Zohei-san has agreed to it, as well.

00:08:31.160 --> 00:08:34.950
Would you be willing to consider 
this a trial arranged marriage?

00:08:35.260 --> 00:08:37.700
Excuse me! You really can't...

00:08:38.180 --> 00:08:40.750
<i>I remain unconvinced.</i>

00:08:40.750 --> 00:08:44.110
<i>And if he does or says 
anything to hurt Botan,</i>

00:08:44.110 --> 00:08:45.710
<i>I'll run him through on the spot!</i>

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:47.340
<i>Could you please not?</i>

00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:53.640
<i>Still, Hyoma-kun's got quite 
a poker face going on.</i>

00:08:53.640 --> 00:08:56.650
<i>I really hope he doesn't lash out.</i>

00:08:56.650 --> 00:08:58.620
<i>I'm so tired.</i>

00:08:59.370 --> 00:09:02.470
<i>How will you respond, Kunato Hyoma?!</i>

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:10.660
You may have received 
my grandfather's assent,

00:09:11.080 --> 00:09:14.080
but your own desires in the matter aside,

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:17.930
I haven't finished getting 
<i>your</i> measure yet.

00:09:18.960 --> 00:09:23.460
This sudden request to join your household 
isn't something I can agree to so easily.

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:28.040
However, it would be disrespectful to 
my grandfather to refuse unconditionally.

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:31.480
Therefore, I will defer judgment for now.

00:09:32.360 --> 00:09:35.300
Well... I suppose that's all right.

00:09:36.310 --> 00:09:37.400
Nagatsuki-san.

00:09:37.400 --> 00:09:38.350
Yes?!

00:09:38.350 --> 00:09:41.080
Wednesdays are my designated running days.

00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:44.220
I would ordinarily leave at this time. May I?

00:09:45.540 --> 00:09:46.730
Go ahead.

00:09:46.730 --> 00:09:48.730
Excellent. I shall return.

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:53.800
That reaction was weird. Too rational.

00:09:53.800 --> 00:09:54.780
Yeah.

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:57.510
He's so calm, it's freaking me out a little.

00:09:58.900 --> 00:10:00.620
Although...

00:10:01.240 --> 00:10:04.170
I've gotta live with the guy another year,

00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:07.750
and now you've gone 
and made it awkward again!

00:10:08.820 --> 00:10:11.250
W-We had good intentions, really...

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:13.880
Besides...

00:10:14.250 --> 00:10:18.600
I just, really... I can't 
<i>do</i> something like that.

00:10:18.600 --> 00:10:20.260
You know that.

00:10:22.670 --> 00:10:26.250
You worry too much. About everything.

00:10:26.730 --> 00:10:31.450
That's what makes us so anxious, you know?

00:10:27.300 --> 00:10:30.340
Ow, ow, ow, ow!

00:10:32.200 --> 00:10:35.260
Still, Hyoma-kun was pretty 
unflappable back there.

00:10:35.260 --> 00:10:38.990
I suppose it's <i>slightly</i> better 
than him throwing a fit.

00:11:00.390 --> 00:11:02.680
Wh-What the hell was that?!

00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:12.100
<i>Yeah, that was not cool.</i>

00:11:12.100 --> 00:11:14.730
I love the whole fish.

00:11:12.950 --> 00:11:14.730
<i>Not cool!</i>

00:11:14.730 --> 00:11:18.670
<i>Springing on a guy who's only 
lived here a few days,</i>

00:11:18.670 --> 00:11:22.610
<i>"Oh, we're actually evaluating you as 
a prospective husband for our daughter!"</i>

00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:26.230
<i>He probably had no idea 
what they were saying.</i>

00:11:27.250 --> 00:11:30.790
<i>I barely knew what I was saying, either.</i>

00:11:38.710 --> 00:11:41.050
Look at how she's torturing herself!

00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:43.590
This could get very interesting!

00:11:45.960 --> 00:11:48.010
What? Time to go out?

00:11:48.010 --> 00:11:48.930
Already?!

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:54.260
Oh, fine.

00:11:56.060 --> 00:11:56.570
I love the whole fish.
Flounder in Sauce

00:11:56.570 --> 00:11:57.440
February

00:11:56.570 --> 00:11:57.440
<b>Lunches\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
 of Happiness</b>

00:11:58.430 --> 00:12:02.310
<i>I've got to find him, apologize, 
and tell him not to worry about it!</i>

00:12:06.130 --> 00:12:07.900
<i>After I go shopping, though.</i>

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:11.920
Haori informed me of the 
arranged marriage condition.

00:12:11.920 --> 00:12:17.500
I have my own guesses as to why 
you agreed to this arrangement.

00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:18.750
May I reveal them?

00:12:18.750 --> 00:12:21.090
<i>Sure, give it a go.</i>

00:12:21.450 --> 00:12:26.410
Create a tense relationship 
to increase my mental fortitude.

00:12:26.410 --> 00:12:29.850
In other words, 
a form of psychological training.

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:31.520
Um, no.

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:33.680
It's just, a man tends to worry 
when his grandson turns 21

00:12:33.680 --> 00:12:37.580
and hasn't shown the slightest 
interest in romance.

00:12:37.580 --> 00:12:38.480
What?

00:12:38.910 --> 00:12:42.090
<i>It was just perfect timing, 
as far as I was concerned!</i>

00:12:42.090 --> 00:12:45.280
<i>Botan-chan's grown into 
quite a lovely young woman,</i>

00:12:45.280 --> 00:12:47.660
<i>so I couldn't think of any reason to re—</i>

00:12:52.240 --> 00:12:53.870
I see.

00:12:55.540 --> 00:12:57.250
Business? With Haori?

00:12:57.600 --> 00:12:58.380
Yes.

00:12:58.800 --> 00:13:00.910
I wish to engage her in earnest discussion.

00:13:00.910 --> 00:13:02.510
Do you know where I might find her?

00:13:02.510 --> 00:13:05.450
She's out with Kushige.

00:13:05.450 --> 00:13:08.010
She could be gone for days.

00:13:08.010 --> 00:13:09.420
A business trip?

00:13:09.890 --> 00:13:12.440
Yeah, she takes them sometimes.

00:13:12.440 --> 00:13:14.390
Did Nagi and Yu accompany her?

00:13:14.390 --> 00:13:18.650
No, they're doing the usual business.

00:13:26.540 --> 00:13:29.320
Apparently that Hikaki guy 
had more people in his gang

00:13:29.320 --> 00:13:31.700
than what we saw the other day.

00:13:34.420 --> 00:13:36.710
Why aren't I out with them now?!

00:13:38.070 --> 00:13:40.460
I thought you were calling home.

00:13:42.900 --> 00:13:44.840
Oh? Hyoma-san?

00:13:46.000 --> 00:13:48.720
I thought you went out with Nagi and Yu!

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:51.320
No, I was left behind.

00:13:52.880 --> 00:13:54.620
Are you going shopping?

00:13:54.620 --> 00:13:56.560
Oh? Yes...

00:13:57.490 --> 00:13:58.980
Hush!

00:14:02.940 --> 00:14:04.860
Um...

00:14:05.480 --> 00:14:07.490
Hyoma-san, I...

00:14:10.850 --> 00:14:13.260
You, uh, don't have to worry 
about any of that stuff they said.

00:14:13.260 --> 00:14:14.540
I know it's just a huge bother...

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:15.610
Indeed.

00:14:17.740 --> 00:14:19.480
It <i>is</i> a huge bother.

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:23.800
You can be assured that I haven't 
given it a moment's concern.

00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:30.890
I see.

00:14:35.890 --> 00:14:36.990
Great.

00:14:36.990 --> 00:14:39.390
I'm glad to hear you're not worried about it.

00:14:39.390 --> 00:14:43.400
But I really do feel bad 
for the trouble, so... sorry!

00:14:43.790 --> 00:14:46.400
Anyway, I really need to 
get that shopping done.

00:14:46.830 --> 00:14:47.780
Understood.

00:14:57.080 --> 00:14:58.440
Hyoma-kun.

00:15:03.700 --> 00:15:06.380
What you did just now wasn't great.

00:15:07.520 --> 00:15:09.880
I merely spoke the truth.

00:15:10.240 --> 00:15:12.300
You could've been more sensitive.

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:16.640
To turn down a girl her age 
with total indifference...

00:15:17.220 --> 00:15:19.670
You can't see how cruel that is?

00:15:21.110 --> 00:15:24.890
I'm a pretty calm guy, but when I see 
you hurt my mistress like that...

00:15:24.890 --> 00:15:28.440
Can you see how much it pains me?

00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:31.220
Meanwhile, Kagami's crying her eyes out!

00:15:31.840 --> 00:15:34.970
You suck, Hyoma-san!

00:15:34.970 --> 00:15:38.300
You don't have to be so mean!

00:15:38.300 --> 00:15:40.990
Botan was really hurt by that!

00:15:40.990 --> 00:15:42.960
Go! Get him!

00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:45.190
Botan was hurt?

00:15:46.340 --> 00:15:47.560
Wait a minute.

00:15:47.560 --> 00:15:49.010
Can you explain what you mean by that?

00:15:59.980 --> 00:16:01.750
It <i>is</i> a huge bother.

00:16:03.970 --> 00:16:06.150
<i>Hearing him say it that clearly,</i>

00:16:07.000 --> 00:16:11.100
<i>I guess I can trust that 
he's not stressing out about it.</i>

00:16:11.100 --> 00:16:13.720
<i>Which is a good thing, but...</i>

00:16:14.380 --> 00:16:18.630
<i>If it's a good thing, 
why does it bug me so much?</i>

00:16:21.170 --> 00:16:24.170
Well, well. Isn't this a find?

00:16:30.570 --> 00:16:34.120
Are those lackeys of yours 
busy elsewhere, perhaps?

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:39.180
<b>— Hainarashi —</b>

00:16:35.720 --> 00:16:38.630
Would you be Nagatsuki Botan, then?

00:16:40.420 --> 00:16:41.740
A decoy, eh?

00:16:44.320 --> 00:16:49.440
Right about now, our boss'll have found 
his way to that powerless mistress of yours!

00:16:50.240 --> 00:16:51.440
What now?

00:16:51.440 --> 00:16:54.450
You guys care about her, don't you?

00:16:54.450 --> 00:16:56.200
What'll you do, eh?!

00:17:02.450 --> 00:17:03.710
Damn it!

00:17:03.710 --> 00:17:04.570
Botan!

00:17:12.270 --> 00:17:16.970
Your family did a number on 
that "little brother" of mine...

00:17:17.430 --> 00:17:19.210
I've been looking for you.

00:17:19.210 --> 00:17:20.970
Would you be willing to come with me?

00:17:21.890 --> 00:17:24.980
You're a tsukumogami too, aren't you?

00:17:25.940 --> 00:17:27.480
You've seen your share of us, then?

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:29.480
You certainly have some backbone.

00:17:29.930 --> 00:17:32.380
But I can also see you trembling.

00:17:33.480 --> 00:17:35.900
Is this all you are?!

00:17:36.940 --> 00:17:41.990
There's a kind of unwritten law among 
the tsukumogami who live in Kyo...

00:17:42.120 --> 00:17:45.750
<b>Don't make use of Nagatsuki Botan</b>

00:17:42.840 --> 00:17:45.750
"Don't make use of Nagatsuki Botan."

00:17:46.240 --> 00:17:49.500
Was that merely a precaution to keep us away?

00:18:03.360 --> 00:18:05.800
I am Hainarashi.

00:18:05.800 --> 00:18:11.110
My only power as a tsukumogami 
is the ability to scatter ash, but...

00:18:12.300 --> 00:18:16.240
I can still tear a human apart easily enough!

00:18:28.980 --> 00:18:30.890
Are you all right, Nagatsuki-san?

00:18:31.460 --> 00:18:32.810
Are you...

00:18:33.210 --> 00:18:34.210
a Saenome?!

00:18:36.920 --> 00:18:40.010
Child... Know your place!

00:18:41.330 --> 00:18:42.750
Found 'em!

00:18:43.830 --> 00:18:45.430
You dumbass!

00:18:46.070 --> 00:18:48.430
You're gonna pay for this!

00:18:49.650 --> 00:18:51.190
Nagi! Yu!

00:18:51.940 --> 00:18:53.560
We're good to go, right?

00:18:53.560 --> 00:18:54.320
Of course!

00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:55.820
Heck yeah!

00:18:56.170 --> 00:18:57.190
Get him!

00:18:57.190 --> 00:18:58.640
Wait!

00:18:58.640 --> 00:18:59.950
Three-on-one...

00:19:00.450 --> 00:19:02.950
That's not fair!

00:19:00.950 --> 00:19:02.950
<b>Kunato</b>

00:19:04.580 --> 00:19:05.950
Shut up!

00:19:08.490 --> 00:19:10.320
H-Hey!

00:19:14.560 --> 00:19:17.010
I'd like an honest answer.

00:19:17.010 --> 00:19:22.160
Did you actually try to eliminate 
me while I was vulnerable?

00:19:22.160 --> 00:19:24.150
No, but...

00:19:26.510 --> 00:19:29.020
Are you all right, Botan?!

00:19:30.070 --> 00:19:33.400
Were you hurt? Did you sprain anything?!

00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:35.820
I... I'm okay!

00:19:35.820 --> 00:19:38.470
You're sure? Let me see...

00:19:36.840 --> 00:19:39.830
I was pretty mad. And I'm sorry.

00:19:40.200 --> 00:19:41.930
And I gotta thank you.

00:19:42.360 --> 00:19:43.570
I'm okay!

00:19:44.180 --> 00:19:46.500
You saved Botan.

00:19:47.640 --> 00:19:49.430
Guess I owe you one.

00:19:51.680 --> 00:19:53.290
Time to head back.

00:19:53.290 --> 00:19:54.460
Why?!

00:19:54.830 --> 00:19:59.230
You just left the decoys 
wrapped up in your hairpins!

00:19:59.230 --> 00:20:01.340
Botan!

00:20:06.790 --> 00:20:07.850
Hyoma-san...

00:20:09.670 --> 00:20:12.970
Thank you... for saving me.

00:20:13.800 --> 00:20:16.840
I merely did the duty of the Saenome.

00:20:17.520 --> 00:20:19.700
But... what were you doing here?

00:20:21.510 --> 00:20:25.800
Go after her! Make her feel better now!

00:20:22.070 --> 00:20:25.800
Kagami requested that I follow you.

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:29.580
She heard all that?!

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:31.780
I'm sorry, Nagatsuki-san.

00:20:32.960 --> 00:20:37.290
The way I spoke in the hallway 
was conducive to misunderstanding.

00:20:39.350 --> 00:20:42.990
Given your reaction to the reveal 
of the arranged marriage agreement,

00:20:42.990 --> 00:20:45.770
it was clear, even to me, 
that the idea upset you.

00:20:46.220 --> 00:20:50.730
I could tell they've been making trouble 
for you in this regard for some time.

00:20:52.980 --> 00:20:59.020
So I simply wanted to tell you... 
not to be overly concerned on my behalf.

00:21:01.780 --> 00:21:04.980
I hope he cleared things up with her, Suzuri.

00:21:05.990 --> 00:21:08.920
How can anyone be so bad 
at expressing themselves?

00:21:09.800 --> 00:21:13.290
And my grandfather was enthusiastically 
complicit in the arrangement...

00:21:13.690 --> 00:21:19.790
But I don't want you to think I lack 
any feeling or interest toward you at all.

00:21:22.720 --> 00:21:26.660
Er... that's not to say I <i>have</i> interest 
toward you... That would sound strange.

00:21:26.660 --> 00:21:31.560
Ah, why is that strange? What have I said?

00:21:32.400 --> 00:21:34.310
Hey, Hyoma-san...

00:21:35.720 --> 00:21:37.310
It sounds like...

00:21:38.100 --> 00:21:42.140
It sounds like we both have 
relatives who like to meddle.

00:21:42.140 --> 00:21:43.400
It's a pain, huh?

00:21:47.950 --> 00:21:49.400
Indeed it is.

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Suspicions</b>
